WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:02.450
- The Constitution of the United States

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:04.760
is a crucial document to understand

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.490
if you're a United States citizen.

00:00:06.490 --> 00:00:09.950
And, frankly, for almost
anyone on the planet,

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:12.760
obviously the United States
is an influential country,

00:00:12.760 --> 00:00:15.850
but beyond that, many of
the countries out there

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.230
constitutions are actually based

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.780
on the United States Constitution.

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:23.750
So in these lessons
we're going to dive deep.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.580
We're actually going to
read the Constitution.

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:29.330
And, as you'll see, we will read alongside

00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.030
some of the top experts of
the United States Constitution

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.430
in the world.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.310
But we'll do it in a
way that you'll realize

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:37.750
that you too can be something of an expert

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:39.400
on the United States Constitution.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:42.330
We're gonna go through all
of the various articles

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.060
and sections of the Constitution.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.570
And you'll find that it's
an intriguing document

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:49.610
that has incredible relevance, even today.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.950
We're also going to talk
about how the judicial system,

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:54.710
in particular the Supreme Court,

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:57.250
has interpreted the
United States Constitution

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.590
and how that has had a
whole chain of side effects

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:02.480
on our everyday lives.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.880
And last but not least,

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:06.980
we're going to talk about
what rights and liberties

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.420
are protected by the Bill of Rights

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.600
inside of the United States Constitution.

00:01:11.600 --> 00:01:13.800
So let's go on this journey together.

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.870
Whether you live in the United States

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.030
and really just wanna understand

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:19.750
the government that you live in

00:01:19.750 --> 00:01:23.390
or you're just a curious
mind wanting to understand

00:01:23.390 --> 00:01:26.100
how a government can be structured,

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.510
these lessons will answer your questions.

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:31.990
And if you wanna learn
more and get deep practice

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:33.105
with immediate feedback,

00:01:33.105 --> 00:01:33.938
(computer chiming)

00:01:33.938 --> 00:01:35.310
I encourage you to look at these lessons

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.353
on khanacademy.org.

